sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor C as Citizen (browser)
    participant CP as Citizen Portal SPA<br/>(client: citizen-portal, :3000)
    participant KC as Keycloak HOSTED PAGE<br/>(:8080, realm: citizens)
    participant NIS as NIS Portal SPA<br/>(client: nis-portal, :3002)
    participant API as Citizen API (:4100)

    Note over CP,NIS: The portal SPAs have NO username/password form.<br/>Credentials are entered ONLY on Keycloak's page at :8080.

    Note over C,KC: FIRST LOGIN — full-page redirect to Keycloak (Auth Code + PKCE)
    C->>CP: open http://localhost:3000
    CP-->>C: keycloak.init(login-required) → redirect browser to Keycloak
    C->>KC: browser now at :8080/.../auth?client_id=citizen-portal&code_challenge=...
    Note over C,KC: User types credentials INTO KEYCLOAK (:8080), not the portal
    alt existing citizen
        C->>KC: enter username + password (on Keycloak)
    else new citizen (self-registration)
        C->>KC: click Register → fill Keycloak registration form → submit
    end
    KC->>KC: authenticate → create realm SSO session<br/>Set-Cookie: KEYCLOAK_IDENTITY (on :8080)
    KC-->>C: redirect browser back to :3000 with ?code=...
    C->>CP: return to portal with ?code
    CP->>KC: POST /token (code + PKCE verifier)  ← SPA only ever sees the code
    KC-->>CP: access + refresh + id tokens
    CP-->>C: render Citizen Portal (SPA never handled the password)

    Note over C,KC: NAVIGATE TO NIS — SILENT SSO (session cookie already on :8080)
    C->>NIS: open http://localhost:3002
    NIS-->>C: keycloak.init(login-required) → redirect to Keycloak
    C->>KC: browser at :8080/authorize?client_id=nis-portal
    KC->>KC: realm session present → NO login page shown
    KC-->>C: redirect back to :3002 with ?code (silent)
    C->>NIS: NIS exchanges code → its own tokens → render (already authenticated)

    Note over C,API: NIS needs EXTRA details (NIS number etc.) — NOT a Keycloak login.<br/>Progressive enrolment on the SAME logged-in user, done in the app.
    NIS-->>C: no NIS_MEMBER in token → show NIS registration form (in the app)
    C->>NIS: enter DOB, employment status, address
    NIS->>API: POST /api/nis/enrol (Bearer citizen token)
    API->>KC: service account → grant NIS_MEMBER to THIS existing user + allocate NIS number
    API-->>NIS: { nisNumber }
    NIS->>KC: keycloak.updateToken(-1) → refresh so token now carries NIS_MEMBER
    NIS-->>C: render NIS dashboard (NIS number + services)
